response.text:
I have fixed the bug in `parse-range.mjs` where a single number input resulted in `to` being `NaN` instead of matching the `from` value. I updated the function to check if `to` is undefined and, if so, set it to the same value as `from`.

```javascript
export function parseRange(text) {
  const [from, to] = text.split("-");
  const fromNum = Number(from);
  return { from: fromNum, to: to === undefined ? fromNum : Number(to) };
}
```

All tests now pass.
